<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Winrich von Kniprode</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1310–1382</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Winrich von Kniprode was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> from 1351 to 1382, a period often regarded as the height of its power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. He strengthened its administration, finances and towns, encouraged learning among the brethren, and led the war against pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanians">Lithuanians</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rudau">Battle of Rudau</a> in 1370.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winrich-von-kniprode.jpg" alt="Winrich von Kniprode" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lestat (Jan Mehlich) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malbork_-_Winrich_von_Kniprode.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
